1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,579
If technology is what
you're talking about,

2
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:41,041
We still don't trust you.

3
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:42,792
But I want to leave this place.

4
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,294
Don't you guys want to establish a signal?

5
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:54,763
<i>Noberto, I know that</i>

6
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:58,058
the safety of your team
and of Sophie is important.

7
00:00:58,141 --> 00:00:59,726
Let me tell you this.

8
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,562
Please bring Angelito and Mikoy home.

9
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:04,981
We have to bring them back safely
for Tess's sake.

10
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,441
Have hope.

11
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,358
Thank you.

12
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:16,534
<i>Thank you for not leaving me.</i>

13
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:19,662
<i>Even though I'm so weak.</i>

14
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>It's nothing.</i>

15
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:27,045
<i>Don't leave me, please!</i>

16
00:01:27,128 --> 00:01:30,006
It doesn't matter who… stay by my side.

17
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:32,884
Sianong!

18
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:36,888
Will you still forgive me?

19
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,149
Come on!

20
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:54,739
Why now of all times?

21
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:09,087
Why now?!

22
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,799
I'll be on guard here.

23
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:25,395
Chiara.

24
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:32,402
I know.

25
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,281
Not only did I fail to get the bomb,

26
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:39,284
we also couldn't catch up
with Sofie and Angelito,

27
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,454
and now we're in the middle of nowhere,

28
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:46,166
while Sianong is fighting for his life.

29
00:02:51,337 --> 00:02:54,257
What a series
of unfortunate events, right?

30
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:57,468
And the worst part is,
we're running out of time.

31
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,470
There's nothing we can do.

32
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:13,359
Angelito, not now.

33
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,452
Is this the end for me?

34
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:24,996
Focus, Sofie.

35
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:27,123
You can do this, Sofie.

36
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:34,839
You can do this.

37
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:39,719
Come on, Angelito.

38
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,251
Here.

39
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:12,335
There are tracks.

40
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,424
They're still here.

41
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:19,467
They couldn't have gone far.

42
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:22,762
There's a house.

43
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:23,846
Come on.

44
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:26,557
Let's check it out.

45
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,121
Chiara.

46
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:31,748
You're not pathetic, okay?

47
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,250
You've done everything you can.

48
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:36,085
Chiara.

49
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,838
You're already doing more than enough.

50
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,176
You're not alone, okay?

51
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,803
Always remember that,

52
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:48,598
and remember what I told you.

53
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:50,933
When the pressure gets too heavy,

54
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,604
we can make it lighter,

55
00:05:55,855 --> 00:05:57,315
just share the burden.

56
00:05:58,941 --> 00:05:59,776
Right?

57
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,654
I'm frustrated too, Chiara,

58
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:07,617
but we can't give up.

59
00:06:09,368 --> 00:06:11,204
For the people we love, right?

60
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:14,957
And we'll never, ever
give up on each other.

61
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:23,716
Anyone home?

62
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,511
Open up unless you want
someone to get hurt.

63
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:31,849
Why does anyone have to get hurt?

64
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,684
What do you need?

65
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,649
Wait a minute. What are you doing here?

66
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,948
We're just looking for someone.

67
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:48,282
Who are you looking for?

68
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:49,617
What do you need?

69
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,623
Oh my.

70
00:06:56,332 --> 00:06:57,583
It's Lady Amor.

71
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,639
Tonight may feel long,

72
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:16,686
but I'm sure
tomorrow will bring the light.

73
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:23,568
Everything will be all right.

74
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,162
I'll always be here for you.

75
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:36,706
No matter what happens.

76
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,133
And remember what I told you.

77
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:49,927
In the darkness,

78
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:53,431
the stars shine the brightest.

79
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:39,060
What are you doing here?

80
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,895
Everyone else has already left.

81
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,813
Why are you still here?

82
00:08:44,148 --> 00:08:45,942
Why would I leave?

83
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,361
I live here. This is my home.

84
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:50,613
So you'll be the only one left
on the island?

85
00:08:54,450 --> 00:09:00,331
Lord, we both know
I'm not exactly a religious girly,

86
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:04,210
but I know You can hear me.

87
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,509
The people here will come back.

88
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:14,220
This is where we were born and raised.

89
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:16,806
This is where we learned how to survive.

90
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:19,475
Whatever disaster comes our way,

91
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:22,895
we always find a way
to get back on our feet.

92
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:31,529
Angelito.

93
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:36,325
Is your guardian angel asleep too?

94
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:43,291
Let's go.

95
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,042
We're getting nowhere here.

96
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:47,587
Let's move.

97
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:41,932
Since we can't control
the variables out there,

98
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:44,060
it's best to come overprepared.

99
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:47,021
So, Team 1, Kian, you'll lead
the front line, so we can get in.

100
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:55,154
And Team 3, Dara and I.

101
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:57,490
We'll look for Mikoy, Chiara, and Sianong.

102
00:10:58,407 --> 00:11:01,285
Mario, you and Ben
will secure the safe house.

103
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,787
Let's make sure it's on high alert.

104
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:08,292
So far, these are the top locations
where they could be.

105
00:11:09,418 --> 00:11:12,922
If we have to search
every inch of this island, we will.

106
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:43,244
There it is.

107
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,370
We've got a signal!

108
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:51,419
We've got a signal!

109
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:52,837
Angelito.

110
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,422
Angelito.

111
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,091
Angelito.

112
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:58,259
Wake up.

113
00:11:59,009 --> 00:11:59,969
That was fast!

114
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:02,012
Prayer answered right away.

115
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,567
Sofie is calling.

116
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,918
Do you ever regret it?

117
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:17,379
Regret what?

118
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,798
This life.

119
00:13:20,716 --> 00:13:23,344
It's dangerous, chaotic,

120
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:26,138
and complicated,
all because you chose Chiara.

121
00:13:33,062 --> 00:13:33,938
You know,

122
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,566
no matter who we choose
to spend our lives with,

123
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:40,236
we all go through hardships.

124
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:43,197
This just happens to be mine.

125
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,241
Ours, mine and Chiara's.

126
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:46,909
That's all.

127
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,287
You have a point, brother.

128
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:53,040
But don't you ever wonder

129
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:56,043
if everything you and Chiara
have fought for is worth it?

130
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:58,420
Everything you're fighting for.

131
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:05,386
But don't you ever ask yourself

132
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,013
what all this is?

133
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:09,890
Is it really worth it?

134
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:23,946
I'm on my way.

135
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:18,125
To answer your question, yes, of course!

136
00:15:18,208 --> 00:15:19,335
It's really worth it, right?

137
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:20,252
It's all worth it.

138
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:27,551
You know,
we haven't yet seen the end of the tunnel.

139
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:29,803
But isn't it true what they say,

140
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:31,597
there's light at the end?

141
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:38,854
Also, they say,
"There's always a rainbow after the rain."

142
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:40,731
Yes, right?

143
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:44,610
There is.

144
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:48,072
But that's not how I know La Fornarina.

145
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:51,450
I really don't see her in that way.

146
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:58,499
That's not how I know Chiara.

147
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:01,043
What I know about Chiara,

148
00:16:01,752 --> 00:16:03,629
there's always an agenda.

149
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:11,512
Should be a mission accomplished.

150
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:13,180
And once she has done that,

151
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:15,432
she leaves everything behind.

152
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:24,566
And if it's a lot, sorry.

153
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:29,738
It can't be!

154
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:32,992
Perhaps it was before,
when we didn't know each other.

155
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,159
But now,

156
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:36,954
not anymore.

157
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:41,417
My sweetheart is different.

158
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:44,294
My goodness!

159
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:50,300
I mean, love really does wonders.

160
00:16:58,475 --> 00:17:01,020
You know, me and Chiara,

161
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:04,773
the meaning of mission accomplished
is clear with us,

162
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:07,651
once our dream lives are within reach.

163
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:09,737
That's all there is.

164
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,448
What?

165
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,658
You'll leave us behind?

166
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:17,244
Like what you did in Hong Kong.

167
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:20,247
You'll create new fake passports.

168
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:22,916
No, we don't have anymore secrets, right?

169
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:28,714
As long as it's just simple,

170
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:31,884
being happy, us two being together.

171
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:38,348
That's what mission accomplished
means to us.

172
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:40,392
And sooner or later,

173
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,227
We'll be close to reaching that.

174
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:44,021
That's it!

175
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:49,026
Now I know why
you're so in love with Chiara.

176
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:52,696
You know, it's so nice
to be witnessing this.

177
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:57,076
I mean, even her priorities have shifted.

178
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:04,041
I understand now that your love…

179
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:08,337
is important for her too.

180
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:12,341
Hopefully I get to witness
your mission accomplished.

181
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,095
Once you achieve the simple life.

182
00:18:19,306 --> 00:18:20,307
Thanks.

183
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,019
Angelito hasn't been responsive
for a long while now.

184
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,605
Will he wake up?

185
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,733
I'm doing everything I can, Sophie.

186
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,865
Just have faith.

187
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:17,716
Agents, stay alert.

188
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:19,676
You all know what to do.

189
00:21:00,384 --> 00:21:02,261
Alex! Dara!

190
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:09,101
Rafa!

191
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:34,751
That's all you've got?!

192
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:40,442
Good. Let's move faster!

193
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:09,429
There!

194
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,186
Hey!

195
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:17,145
That was a gunshot.

196
00:23:18,980 --> 00:23:20,190
My gun too!

197
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:42,462
Could that be Agent Alex?

198
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:44,631
Maybe rescue is here.

199
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:47,717
Or maybe it's La Morte Bianca.

200
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,720
She sent reinforcements to finish us off.

201
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:54,558
What's important is we're ready, okay?

202
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:12,826
How's your wound?

203
00:24:12,909 --> 00:24:13,743
It's just a graze, ma'am.

204
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:36,725
Who is it?

205
00:24:37,225 --> 00:24:38,268
There's more.

206
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:45,192
- Hold your fire! It's us.
- It's them!

207
00:24:45,275 --> 00:24:46,234
Wait.

208
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:00,248
Sianong?

209
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:01,833
Sianong!

210
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:05,670
Duh!

211
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:33,531
Angelito, wake up!

212
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:34,908
Help!

213
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:37,369
Help!

214
00:25:39,829 --> 00:25:42,540
<i>All these lives are on the line</i>
<i>because of me.</i>

215
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:46,586
But that's the truth, sir.

216
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:49,631
If I'd just listened,
all this wouldn't have happened.
